# 09:00 Riyadh, daily — both halves chosen, neither inherited.
#
# WHY DAILY. The check is cheap and almost always decides «nothing to do»: it
# acts only when five days or fewer remain (REFRESH_MARGIN_DAYS), and a Salla
# access token lives one to two weeks. Daily is what turns that margin into a
# retry budget — six attempts (5, 4, 3, 2, 1, 0 days left) before the
# credential dies, so a Salla outage, a DNS blip or a host that was switched
# off costs nothing at all.
#
#   Weekly was rejected outright: with a five-day margin a weekly timer gets
#   AT MOST ONE attempt inside it, so a single failed Sunday is the whole
#   incident again, with a cron entry to point at afterwards.
#
#   Hourly was rejected too. It buys nothing — the margin is measured in days
#   and the token's life is measured in weeks — while multiplying by
#   twenty-four the exposure to the one thing that is unrecoverable: Salla's
#   refresh tokens are SINGLE-USE, and two exchanges racing each other make
#   its OAuth server revoke everything and require the merchant to reinstall
#   the app. The script holds a lock against exactly that, and a schedule that
#   leans on a lock twenty-four times a day for no benefit is a bad trade.
#
# WHY 09:00. Two constraints, and they agree.
#   * It is inside Fahad's working hours. When this job gives up, the only
#     recovery in existence is HIM reinstalling the app on his store — the
#     Easy Mode credential is never shown to a human, so there is nothing to
#     paste and nothing a server can do. An alert that lands at 03:30 next to
#     the backup is an alert he reads after the credential is dead.
#   * It is two hours before the 11:00 nightly run. A credential renewed in
#     the morning is already in place when the delivery run reads it, and the
#     nightly run's own boot check becomes the second, independent witness the
#     same day rather than the next one.
#
# Persistent=true, for the same reason career-backup.timer has it: a machine
# that was off at 09:00 is precisely the machine whose credential quietly aged
# another day, and catching up is harmless — a caught-up run outside the
# margin still decides «nothing to do».
[Unit]
Description=Daily Salla credential refresh at 09:00 Riyadh

[Timer]
OnCalendar=*-*-* 09:00:00 Asia/Riyadh
Persistent=true

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
